README 
#       2-Link Robot Planner, Qt version
#
#       Author:  John Paul Ryan
#       Date: August 2015
#
#       $Id:$
# ################################################################################


In the Summer of 2015, John Ryan and Bryant Curto
received a NYU Computer Science Department undergraduate
research grant to work on this robotics project under the supervision
of Professor Yap.  They converted the disc Demo of Cong Wang,
and the 2-links Demos (both the crossing and non-crossing version)
of Zhongdi Luo into a Qt Project.  The previous versions were based
on GLUT/GLUI which was deprecated in MacOS, and OpenGL 2.0.
This new version is in OpenGL 4.0.  This resulted in much faster animation.


Usage: 
	1. Fire up Qt Creator (it should have OpenGL 4.0 or later)
	2. Open the file 2-link.pro in this directory
	3. Compile and run!


